## 2026-08-21 - STEP 16 (CIC-IDS-2017 loader — real flow keys for the engine)
- what: cicids.py loader maps CIC-IDS-2017 ML-format CSV into stream keys the SketchFlow engine can ingest. why: until now, every benchmark used synthetic Zipfian streams — step 16 proves the engine works on REAL intrusion-detection traffic, answering "which destination ports see the most flows?" on actual CICFlowMeter-exported data. concept: mapping real network records to stream keys — the translation layer between a domain-specific dataset and a general-purpose streaming sketch. next: step 17 (HUMAN: fetch one MAWI daily pcap for backbone traffic analysis).
- design notes: the CIC-IDS-2017 MachineLearningCSV format has NO raw IP addresses or protocol field (it's an ML-ready export of CICFlowMeter features). Destination Port is the only network-header column, so the loader builds keys as "port:<N>" (e.g. "port:80", "port:443"). This answers the natural network-monitoring question: "which services are targeted most?" Two entry points: load_cicids() yields simple keys for the engine; load_cicids_flows() yields rich dicts with port, label, duration, and packet counts for deeper analysis.
- key findings from first real-data run: 10180 flows, 1371 distinct destination ports. DNS (port 53) dominates at 3667 flows, HTTP (80) at 2990, HTTPS (443) at 1696. The engine's top-10 ports match the exact baseline perfectly with k=500 Space-Saving headroom and ε=0.001. CU-CMS reduces total overestimation vs plain CMS on real traffic (same result as on synthetic data — the CU advantage is real, not an artifact of Zipfian shape). Never-undercount invariant holds for all 1371 ports. Web-attack flows (Brute Force, XSS, SQL Injection) cluster on port 80 as expected.
- gate design note: core gate (plan.json): engine top-k matches exact top-k on sample. With 1371 distinct ports and small-count ports at tail positions (7th–10th: counts 15–27), Space-Saving needs k >> distinct-count for tail accuracy. Used k=500 (guarantee threshold N/k ≈ 20, covering all top-10). Also verified: never-undercount for all 1371 keys; CU < CMS overestimation; label distribution matches known composition (8000 benign + 2180 attacks); attack flows target port 80. 17 new tests, 160 total green.
- Commit 50daf4c, CI 1m14s.

